    <value>Done. These are suggestions from one measurement, not certainties.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MappingNoSensors" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No motherboard temperatures found. Start the application as administrator.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MappingNotConnected" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Probably not connected: the readings are implausible.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MappingConstant" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Did not change at all. Possibly unconnected or a fixed value.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MappingFollowsCpu" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Rose almost like the CPU: probably the CPU socket or a CPU temperature input.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MappingWarmsWithCpu" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Warmed up noticeably with CPU load: probably near the voltage regulators (VRM) or the socket.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MappingIndependentOfCpu" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Barely reacted to CPU load: probably chipset, PCIe slot, board or case air, or an external probe.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MappingUnknown" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cannot be judged, because the CPU temperature did not rise enough.</value>
  </data>
